# Cursor — project instructions

This repository uses a cross-agent operating system so work done by Cursor, Claude Code, Gemini
CLI, and Codex stays in sync without any of them sharing memory. Before writing any code, read
and follow `.ai/BOOTSTRAP.md` in full.

That procedure has you read `.ai/PROJECT.md`, `.ai/STATE.md`, `.ai/TASKS.md`, and
`.ai/ARCHITECTURE.md`; check `.ai/FILE_INDEX.md` before creating any file; and produce a short
plan before coding. It also defines exactly when to stop and ask instead of guessing.

Before ending the session, run `.ai/SHUTDOWN.md` in full. It updates the task board, file
index, and changelog, and writes a session record under `.ai/sessions/` so the next agent — in
this tool or a different one — can pick up without anyone re-explaining anything.

Hard constraints that apply on every task: `.ai/RULES.md`.

Full system map: `.ai/README.md`.
